2026-08-16T11:42:00Z    [HD:Net sales] GATE critic: Your derivation is internally inconsistent. You write FY2025Q2 (45,277) × (1 + median YoY growth +0.60%), and you state the median YoY growth is +0.60%. That expression adds 0.60% twice (total +1.20%), which would yield 45,277 × 1.012 = 45,820.3 USDm. The proposed value 45,550.2 USDm corresponds to applying only a single +0.60% (45,277 × 1.006 ≈ 45,548.7). Either the formula is wrong or the computed value is; as written, the number is too low relative to the stated formula.
2026-08-16T11:42:16Z    [DE:Worldwide net sales and revenues] GATE critic: You applied a +12.05% YoY uplift taken from FY2022Q3→FY2023Q3 (+12.0%) to the FY2025Q3 base of $12,018m to estimate FY2026Q3. That’s the wrong period/basis: the relevant comparator is FY2025Q3→FY2026Q3 (or at least the immediate FY2024Q3→FY2025Q3 trend, which Deere reported as −9% YoY to $12,018m). Using a boom-year 2022→2023 growth rate to project 2026 mechanically overstates “Worldwide net sales and revenues.”
2026-08-16T11:42:29Z    [HAS:Pre-exceptional operating profit] tables=0 chunks=18 llm_returned=11 llm_kept=11 rejected_unverifiable_quotes=0 rejected_out_of_band=0 total_facts=11
2026-08-16T11:42:34Z    [HD:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: Your anchor is on the wrong basis: the cited $4.68 for FY2025 Q2 is Home Depot’s GAAP diluted EPS, not an “adjusted” (non‑GAAP) EPS. Home Depot’s Q2 FY2025 press materials do not present an adjusted EPS figure to anchor to. Using a GAAP number while labeling it “adjusted” makes the FY2026 Q2 adjusted EPS projection basis-inconsistent and invalid.
