2026-08-16T11:43:32Z    [ADI:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: The anchor is tied to a “FY2026Q3 adjusted EPS guidance $3.30 ± $0.15,” but ADI does not publish guidance that far ahead; it only guides for the upcoming quarter. That $3.30 range is almost certainly for a different quarter (e.g., FY2025 Q3) and has been misapplied to FY2026 Q3, so the 3.32763 EPS is anchored to the wrong period.
2026-08-16T11:43:34Z    [DE:Diluted EPS (GAAP)] GATE critic: Wrong basis: The model says “post‑guidance signal: none found,” but Deere routinely provides and updates full‑year guidance, and by Q2 FY2026 (May 2026) it had issued FY2026 net income guidance in its earnings release/8‑K. Projecting FY2026Q3 GAAP diluted EPS by applying a median of historical YoY EPS changes to FY2025Q3 (4.75) without reconciling to that FY2026 full‑year guidance is an invalid basis and likely yields a quarterly EPS inconsistent with the company’s guided full‑year outcome. This can be checked directly against Deere’s Q2 FY2026 earnings materials.
2026-08-16T11:43:40Z    [HD:Comparable sales, total company] GATE critic: The stated weighted blend doesn’t equal the proposed value. Using your inputs: 2.46667 × 0.901 = 2.22246967 and 0.15 × 0.099 = 0.01485; sum = 2.23731967%, not 2.23826%. The proposal is ~0.00094 percentage points (~0.094 bps) too high versus its own formula.
