2026-08-16T11:44:29Z    [HAS:Net fees] GATE critic: The -1.25% “post‑guidance signal tilt” is being applied to FY2026 net fees off Q3 FY2025 near‑term (Q4) commentary, and it references a “FY26 net fees guidance midpoint” that the company hasn’t issued (Hays typically guides profit, not net fees). That’s a wrong‑period, wrong‑basis adjustment which artificially drags the forecast from ~£842.8m to £832.2m. You can verify this against Hays’ FY2025 Q3 trading update and FY2025 results, which discuss near‑term trading but do not provide FY2026 net fee guidance to anchor such a tilt.
2026-08-16T11:44:44Z    [ADI:Adjusted gross margin] GATE critic: You double-counted FY2025Q3. The “last 4 reported” average of 70.85% already includes FY2025Q3 (69.2%), and then you averaged that set again with FY2025Q3 to get 70.025%. That gives FY2025Q3 a 5/8 weight and each of the other three quarters only 1/8, arbitrarily biasing the result. With 69.2% below the 70.85% four‑quarter mean, this construction likely pulls the forecast down versus a correctly weighted approach.
