2026-08-16T11:44:53Z    [HAS:Pre-exceptional basic EPS] GATE critic: The proposed FY2026 pre-exceptional basic EPS of 36.4672 GBp is on the wrong scale versus the provided FY2025 pre-exceptional basic EPS of 1.31p (GBp). That implies a >2,600% (≈27–28x) year-on-year jump, which is not supported by any source and strongly suggests a unit/decimal error or an unsourced anchor (the 37.62 input) in the wrong units.
2026-08-16T11:45:08Z    [DE:Production & Precision Ag operating profit] GATE critic: Over-precision: Deere reports segment operating profit to the nearest $1 million, and your anchor ($580m) and growth rates are themselves rounded. Publishing 378.204 (i.e., $378.204m, with $1,000 precision) implies accuracy the inputs cannot support. At minimum this should be rounded to USDm with no decimals (≈$378m), otherwise the figure is misleading on a unit/basis level.
